Bits.Description:
XIP lane format. Selects the configured command/address/data lane pattern used for reads. Must match the currently configured flash state; firmware enters or exits QPI separately through indirect commands.

Usage: Set before enabling XIP.

Values:
0x0 1-1-1;
0x1 1-1-2;
0x2 1-2-2;
0x3 1-1-4;
0x4 1-4-4;
0x5 4-4-4;
0x6 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Indirect address byte count. Selects no address, three-byte address or four-byte address. Use the encoding required by the chosen flash instruction.

Usage: Program before setting start.

Values:
0x0 no address;
0x1 three address bytes;
0x2 four address bytes;
0x3 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Indirect lane format. Selects one of the supported command/address/data lane patterns. Use for standard, dual, quad and QPI indirect transactions in controller role.

Usage: Program before setting start.

Values:
0x0 1-1-1;
0x1 1-1-2;
0x2 1-2-2;
0x3 1-1-4;
0x4 1-4-4;
0x5 4-4-4;
0x6 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.

Error code. Reports the last selected command-engine or FIFO error class. Software reads the code with qspi_irq_raw and command status.

Usage: Reset or a new operation clears the code according to the resolved error policy.

Values:
0x0 no error;
0x1 command/profile error;
0x2 TX FIFO error;
0x3 RX FIFO error;
0x4 flash error;
0x5 to 0x7 reserved.

Unit: none.

Limits: none.
